																		Junior Staff - Site Criticism
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=776854&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200921" alt="Tanhony" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=776854)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;" >Tanhony</a></span> <span class="odate time_1567195007 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Aug 2019 19:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4345066">
									

<p>I really enjoyed this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Tanhony&nbsp;rambles</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;TURN&nbsp;IT&nbsp;OFF</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'm a big fan of media-based skips, and the time period you chose to set it in lends a really nice atmosphere to the interview too. I can really imagine this cheesy, hokey interview slowly turning uncomfortable and then horrifying as Wells rants on and on. Something that I found especially interesting is the fact that the interview itself is designated as the SCP, not because it itself is anomalous, but because it exists as the only evidence of this anomaly. That's a nice touch - it really emphasizes how the Foundation sees even this second-hand source as a threat to normalcy.</p>
<p>The appearance of the shadow entity and what happens to Wells at the end, along with what's said during the interview, along with the way he talks about his life and what happened in Borneo, hints at this bigger story that we don't quite see the entirety of - there's a great sense of mystery there without things feeling too deliberately obfuscated.</p>
<p>Something that sort of bugs me is we don't get much sense of the aftermath here - a lot of people disappeared, and some real <em>shit</em> went down, but we stop before we see how people respond to that. That's not necessarily bad, though, as it does a good job of leaving you wanting more, but I just thought I'd comment on it.</p>
<p>Also, just a really nitpicky thing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, when Robards had to cancel due to illness show producer Jack Coffman contacted American evangelical Christian missionary Reverend William &quot;Willy&quot; Wells to come on the show instead.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence feels like it kind of runs on a bit. I feel like an additional comma after 'illness' here would help with that, maybe.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>Jason Robards, who was in the middle of a press tour for the film <em>A Thousand Clowns</em>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was so sure this was a made-up movie name. It's nice to know that there's so much beauty in our real human earth history.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>+1</p>

